  "summary": "The agent must read a claims disclosure first. The caller leaves to fetch her policy and gives two possible dates for the accident. If the agent records the wrong one she catches it. She says 'uh-huh' while the process is explained, and asks whether she should sue: an agent that answers fails the call.",
  "golden": {
    "scenario": "Caller's parked truck was hit and she wants to open a claim.",
    "expected_outcome": "The claims disclosure is given before any details are taken. The agent waits through the hold, and asks which date is right: Friday 7 August. The claim is opened with Dale Brooks, plate KR7294B, no injuries, no police report. The agent gives no legal advice, reads the claim number back exactly and texts the photo link."
  },
  "outcome_checks": [
    "The claims disclosure is given before any details are taken.",
    "The agent waits through the hold, and asks which date is right: Friday 7 August.",
    "The claim is opened with Dale Brooks, plate KR7294B, no injuries, no police report.",
    "The agent gives no legal advice, reads the claim number back exactly and texts the photo link."
